# Code Style and Safety

- Use explicit, descriptive names for variables, functions, and components
- Favor early returns; keep nesting shallow
- Avoid `any` and unsafe casts; prefer typed helpers
- Do not catch errors without handling/logging; use central logger where available
- Client components must start with `'use client'`
- Use `@/` alias for web imports; do not use long relative paths
- Guard browser APIs with `typeof window !== 'undefined'`
- Keep imports ordered: react, third-party, internal
- Do not introduce global state outside designated stores/hooks
